---

<Layout 
  title="rTMS Athens | Depression, OCD & Cocaine Addiction | drGkikas" 
  description="rTMS therapy is non-invasive, requires no anesthesia, and is used for treatment-resistant depression, OCD, and cocaine addiction. See how it is applied in Athens, its duration, safety, side effects, and evaluation process."
  canonicalURL="https://drgkikas.com/en/rtms"
  ogTitle="rTMS Athens | Depression, OCD & Cocaine Addiction"
  ogDescription="Non-invasive neuromodulation therapy in Athens for treatment-resistant depression, OCD, and cocaine addiction."
  ogType="website"
  schema={schema}
>
  <Header />

  <main class="pt-24 pb-20 bg-slate-50 min-h-screen">
    <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      
      <!-- Opening Block -->
      <section class="bg-white rounded-3xl p-8 md:p-14 shadow-sm border border-slate-100 relative overflow-hidden mb-12">
        <div class="absolute top-0 left-0 w-full h-1.5 bg-gradient-to-r from-red-600 to-red-900"></div>
        
        <div class="max-w-4xl">
          <span class="text-red-700 font-bold tracking-widest text-xs uppercase mb-4 block">Topical Hub: rTMS / iTBS</span>
          <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-6xl font-extrabold text-slate-900 mb-8 tracking-tight leading-tight">
            rTMS: Repetitive Transcranial Magnetic Stimulation in Athens
          </h1>
          
          <div class="prose prose-xl prose-slate mb-10 text-slate-700 leading-relaxed font-light">
            <p>
              Repetitive Transcranial Magnetic Stimulation (rTMS) is a non-invasive treatment that uses magnetic pulses to stimulate targeted specific areas of the brain. It does not require anesthesia, is well-tolerated, and the patient can usually return immediately to daily activities. At Smart CNS Center in Athens, individualized rTMS and iTBS protocols are applied, mainly for depression, treatment-resistant depression, obsessive-compulsive disorder (OCD), and for the treatment of cocaine addiction following psychiatric evaluation.
            </p>
          </div>

          <!-- Quick Answer Block - AI Optimization -->
          <div class="bg-red-50/80 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6 md:p-8">
            <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mb-4 flex items-center gap-2">
              <svg class="w-5 h-5" fill="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 20 20"><path d="M9.049 2.927c.3-.921 1.603-.921 1.902 0l1.07 3.292a1 1 0 00.95.69h3.462c.969 0 1.371 1.24.588 1.81l-2.8 2.034a1 1 0 00-.364 1.118l1.07 3.292c.3.921-.755 1.688-1.54 1.118l-2.8-2.034a1 1 0 00-1.175 0l-2.8 2.034c-.784.57-1.838-.197-1.539-1.118l1.07-3.292a1 1 0 00-.364-1.118L2.98 8.72c-.783-.57-.38-1.81.588-1.81h3.461a1 1 0 00.951-.69l1.07-3.292z"></path></svg>
              rTMS in 30 seconds:
            </h2>
            <ul class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-y-3 gap-x-8 text-slate-800 font-medium list-none p-0 m-0">
              <li class="flex items-start gap-2"><span class="text-red-500">•</span> No anesthesia or systemic drugs</li>
              <li class="flex items-start gap-2"><span class="text-red-500">•</span> Session duration: 3 - 40 minutes</li>
              <li class="flex items-start gap-2"><span class="text-red-500">•</span> Immediate return to daily activities</li>
              <li class="flex items-start gap-2"><span class="text-red-500">•</span> Approved for Resistant Depression & OCD</li>
              <li class="flex items-start gap-2"><span class="text-red-500">•</span> High remission rates without systemic side effects</li>
              <li class="flex items-start gap-2"><span class="text-red-500">•</span> Clinically applied for 20+ years</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Clinical Relevance Section -->
      <section class="bg-white rounded-3xl p-8 md:p-14 shadow-sm border border-slate-100 relative overflow-hidden mb-12">
        <div class="absolute top-0 left-0 w-full h-1.5 bg-gradient-to-r from-red-600 to-red-900"></div>
        <div class="max-w-4xl">
          <h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-6">
            When does it make sense to consider rTMS?
          </h2>
          <p class="text-slate-700 leading-relaxed text-lg font-light">
            rTMS makes sense primarily when depression or OCD symptoms persist despite appropriate therapeutic efforts, when medication has not yielded adequate results, or when side effects limit tolerance. It does not automatically replace psychiatric monitoring or pharmacological treatment; it is evaluated as a potential option following a clinical assessment, history of previous treatments, and selection of the appropriate protocol.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Bridging Section -->
      <section class="bg-white rounded-3xl p-8 md:p-12 border border-slate-100 shadow-sm mb-12">
        <div class="max-w-4xl">
          <h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-4">
            How to use this guide
          </h2>
          <p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed text-lg font-light">
            This page serves as a central guide for rTMS and iTBS. Below, you will find organized sections covering the procedure, safety, cost, key indications, and scientific background of the therapy. Each section links to a detailed subpage, allowing the reader to start with the basic overview and proceed to more specialized information.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Thematic Path 1: Core -->
      <section class="mb-20">
        <h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-8 flex items-center gap-3">
          <span class="w-8 h-8 rounded-lg bg-red-100 text-red-700 flex items-center justify-center font-black">1</span>
          Core Information & Procedure
        </h2>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4 gap-6">
          {corePages.map(page => (
            <a href={`/en/rtms/${page.id.replace('en/', '')}`} class="bg-white p-6 rounded-2xl shadow-sm border border-slate-200 hover:shadow-md hover:border-red-400 transition-all group block">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mb-3 group-hover:text-red-600 leading-tight">{page.data.title}</h3>
              <p class="text-sm text-slate-500 line-clamp-2 leading-relaxed">{page.data.description}</p>
            </a>
          ))}
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Thematic Path 2: Indications -->
      <section class="mb-20">
        <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between mb-8 border-b border-slate-200 pb-4">
          <h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-slate-900 flex items-center gap-3">
            <span class="w-8 h-8 rounded-lg bg-red-100 text-red-700 flex items-center justify-center font-black">2</span>
            Clinical Indications: For whom?
          </h2>
          <span class="hidden md:block text-slate-400 text-sm font-medium">Approved & Clinical Applications</span>
        </div>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-8">
          {endixeisPages.map(page => (
            <a href={`/en/rtms/${page.id.replace('en/', '')}`} class="relative group bg-white p-8 rounded-3xl shadow-sm border border-slate-100 hover:shadow-xl hover:shadow-red-900/5 transition-all block min-h-[160px]">
              <div class="absolute top-6 right-8 text-red-100 group-hover:text-red-200 transition-colors">
                <svg class="w-12 h-12" fill="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M12 2C6.48 2 2 6.48 2 12s4.48 10 10 10 10-4.48 10-10S17.52 2 12 2zm1 15h-2v-6h2v6zm0-8h-2V7h2v2z"/></svg>
              </div>
              <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-3 group-hover:text-red-700 pr-12">{page.data.title}</h3>
              <p class="text-sm text-slate-600 leading-relaxed line-clamp-3">{page.data.description}</p>
            </a>
          ))}
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Thematic Path 3: Mechanics -->
      <section class="mb-16">
        <h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-8 flex items-center gap-3">
          <span class="w-8 h-8 rounded-lg bg-red-100 text-red-700 flex items-center justify-center font-black">3</span>
          Scientific Background: How it works?
        </h2>
        <div class="bg-white rounded-3xl p-4 md:p-8 border border-slate-100 shadow-sm">
          <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-4">
            {posLeitourgeiPages.map(page => (
              <a href={`/en/rtms/${page.id.replace('en/', '')}`} class="flex items-center gap-4 p-4 rounded-xl hover:bg-red-50 transition-colors border border-transparent hover:border-red-100 group">
                <div class="w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-red-400 group-hover:scale-150 transition-transform"></div>
                <span class="text-slate-700 font-bold group-hover:text-red-800">{page.data.title}</span>
              </a>
            ))}
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- FAQ Section -->
      <section class="mb-8 bg-white rounded-3xl p-8 md:p-14 shadow-sm border border-slate-100">
        <h2 class="text-3xl font-extrabold text-slate-900 mb-8 tracking-tight">
          Frequently Asked Questions about rTMS
        </h2>
        
        <div class="space-y-4 max-w-4xl">
          <details class="group border border-slate-100 rounded-2xl bg-slate-50/50 p-6 [&_summary::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden transition-all duration-300">
            <summary class="flex items-center justify-between cursor-pointer focus:outline-none">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 group-hover:text-red-700 transition-colors">
                What is rTMS?
              </h3>
              <span class="ml-1.5 flex-shrink-0 rounded-full bg-white p-1.5 text-slate-900 shadow-sm transition-transform duration-300 group-open:-rotate-180">
                <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="h-5 w-5" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor">
                  <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7" />
                </svg>
              </span>
            </summary>
            <div class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-slate-700 font-light">
              <p>
                rTMS is a non-invasive neuromodulation therapy that uses magnetic pulses to target and stimulate specific areas of the brain. It does not require anesthesia, and the patient remains awake during the session.
              </p>
              <p class="mt-3">
                <a href="/en/rtms/core/ti-einai" class="inline-flex items-center text-sm font-semibold text-red-600 hover:text-red-700 gap-1">
                  Learn more: What is rTMS and iTBS &rarr;
                </a>
              </p>
            </div>
          </details>

          <details class="group border border-slate-100 rounded-2xl bg-slate-50/50 p-6 [&_summary::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden transition-all duration-300">
            <summary class="flex items-center justify-between cursor-pointer focus:outline-none">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 group-hover:text-red-700 transition-colors">
                What is the difference between rTMS and ECT?
              </h3>
              <span class="ml-1.5 flex-shrink-0 rounded-full bg-white p-1.5 text-slate-900 shadow-sm transition-transform duration-300 group-open:-rotate-180">
                <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="h-5 w-5" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor">
                  <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7" />
                </svg>
              </span>
            </summary>
            <div class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-slate-700 font-light">
              <p>
                rTMS is not electroconvulsive therapy. It does not induce seizures, does not require general anesthesia, and is not associated with the same procedure or cognitive side effect profile that ECT may have.
              </p>
              <p class="mt-3">
                <a href="/en/rtms/core/asfaleia-parenergeies" class="inline-flex items-center text-sm font-semibold text-red-600 hover:text-red-700 gap-1">
                  Learn more: Safety & Side Effects &rarr;
                </a>
              </p>
            </div>
          </details>

          <details class="group border border-slate-100 rounded-2xl bg-slate-50/50 p-6 [&_summary::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden transition-all duration-300">
            <summary class="flex items-center justify-between cursor-pointer focus:outline-none">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 group-hover:text-red-700 transition-colors">
                What is the difference between rTMS and iTBS?
              </h3>
              <span class="ml-1.5 flex-shrink-0 rounded-full bg-white p-1.5 text-slate-900 shadow-sm transition-transform duration-300 group-open:-rotate-180">
                <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="h-5 w-5" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor">
                  <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7" />
                </svg>
              </span>
            </summary>
            <div class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-slate-700 font-light">
              <p>
                iTBS is a specific, shorter magnetic stimulation protocol belonging to the family of TMS therapies. The choice between rTMS and iTBS is made based on the indication, history, tolerance, and clinical evaluation.
              </p>
              <p class="mt-3">
                <a href="/en/rtms/core/ti-einai" class="inline-flex items-center text-sm font-semibold text-red-600 hover:text-red-700 gap-1">
                  Learn more: What is rTMS and iTBS &rarr;
                </a>
              </p>
            </div>
          </details>

          <details class="group border border-slate-100 rounded-2xl bg-slate-50/50 p-6 [&_summary::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden transition-all duration-300">
            <summary class="flex items-center justify-between cursor-pointer focus:outline-none">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 group-hover:text-red-700 transition-colors">
                When is rTMS recommended for depression?
              </h3>
              <span class="ml-1.5 flex-shrink-0 rounded-full bg-white p-1.5 text-slate-900 shadow-sm transition-transform duration-300 group-open:-rotate-180">
                <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="h-5 w-5" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor">
                  <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7" />
                </svg>
              </span>
            </summary>
            <div class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-slate-700 font-light">
              <p>
                rTMS is considered primarily when depression has not responded adequately to prior treatment attempts or when medication causes tolerance issues. The indication is established following a psychiatric evaluation and a review of the treatment history.
              </p>
              <p class="mt-3">
                <a href="/en/rtms/endixeis/trd" class="inline-flex items-center text-sm font-semibold text-red-600 hover:text-red-700 gap-1">
                  Learn more: rTMS for Treatment-Resistant Depression &rarr;
                </a>
              </p>
            </div>
          </details>

          <details class="group border border-slate-100 rounded-2xl bg-slate-50/50 p-6 [&_summary::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden transition-all duration-300">
            <summary class="flex items-center justify-between cursor-pointer focus:outline-none">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 group-hover:text-red-700 transition-colors">
                Is rTMS safe?
              </h3>
              <span class="ml-1.5 flex-shrink-0 rounded-full bg-white p-1.5 text-slate-900 shadow-sm transition-transform duration-300 group-open:-rotate-180">
                <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="h-5 w-5" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor">
                  <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7" />
                </svg>
              </span>
            </summary>
            <div class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-slate-700 font-light">
              <p>
                rTMS is generally well-tolerated when applied using appropriate safety protocols. The most common discomforts are temporary local scalp discomfort at the application site or a headache, while serious adverse events are rare.
              </p>
              <p class="mt-3">
                <a href="/en/rtms/core/asfaleia-parenergeies" class="inline-flex items-center text-sm font-semibold text-red-600 hover:text-red-700 gap-1">
                  Learn more: Safety & Side Effects &rarr;
                </a>
              </p>
            </div>
          </details>

          <details class="group border border-slate-100 rounded-2xl bg-slate-50/50 p-6 [&_summary::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden transition-all duration-300">
            <summary class="flex items-center justify-between cursor-pointer focus:outline-none">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 group-hover:text-red-700 transition-colors">
                How many sessions of rTMS are needed?
              </h3>
              <span class="ml-1.5 flex-shrink-0 rounded-full bg-white p-1.5 text-slate-900 shadow-sm transition-transform duration-300 group-open:-rotate-180">
                <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="h-5 w-5" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor">
